<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jani Khan Qashqai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jani Khan was the paramount chief of the Qashqai, the Turkic-speaking nomadic confederation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars province</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. The son of Jani Agha, who rose to prominence under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a>, he was recognised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fath-ali-shah-qajar">Fath Ali Shah</a> as ilkhan of the Qashqai in 1818. His family, the Shahilu, led the confederation into the 20th century.</p></div>
